                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_122">Canterbury,
                            Kent, Benedictine abbey of St Augustine (originally of St Peter and St
                            Paul)</orgName> <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition
                            of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in
                            the Supplement (1987). No corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                            Britain index card was found during data reconciliation work on in
                            2026.</p><p>Compare the rejected entry for this manuscript in B. C.
                            Barker-Benfield (ed.), <title>St. Augustine's Abbey, Canterbury</title>,
                            CMBLC 13, 3 vols (London, 2008), vol. 3, p. 1828: <q>Included under StA
                            at <title>ALCD</title> p. 531 (cf. 504) [...] <title>ALCD</title> cites
                            H. Bradshaw, <title>Collected Papers</title> (Cambridge 1889), 486
                            [recte 485], where the Asser text at art. 1 [...] is attributed to StA.
                            This part of Otho A.xii is entirely lost. However, in 1864 seven leaves
                            were mistakenly restored to it [...] Bradshaw's reference elsewhere
                            (467) to <q>seven remaining leaves</q> of Asser in Otho A.xii shows that
                            he hadd accordingly been misled, though in any case he fails to provide
                            any supporting evidence of his attribution of the Asser (or Æthelweard)
                            to StA.</q></p></provenance>
                    </history>
